<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1733" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">albūgo</span></b> , ĭnis,
			f.
		albus (perh. only in Pliny). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A white spot</i>, <i>a disease of the
				eye; film</i>, <i>albugo</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 32, 7,
				24, § 70</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculorum albugines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					24, 5, 11, § 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pupillarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					29, 6, 38, § 117</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">habere in oculo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Lev. 21, 20</span></i>
			.—*</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In the plur., <i>scurf upon
				the head</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 26, 15, 90, §
		160</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
